// @run
// @log 7
// THE FLOOR THIS FILE PINNED IS LIFTED, and the name is kept so the two cross-references
// and the CHANGELOG entry that name it still resolve — the same graduation
// `variant-annotated-global-floor.vl` beside it already made.
//
// WHAT IT PINNED. `const c = { r: 7 }` is un-annotated in a union program, and
// `globalKind`'s `ObjLit` arm gave a module GLOBAL the union BOX where the identical six
// characters inside a `function` bind the bare ARM. `lamc`'s parameter is the bare arm, and
// `emitCallRef` has a `union`-parameter arm (`emitUnionBoxArg`, which BOXES an un-boxed
// member) and no `variant`-parameter one — so the box would have been pushed raw into a
// `(ref $uVarHeap[vi])` slot. D196 made the call site reachable at all (before it, the
// `(Circle) => Circle` annotation keyed a struct row that does not exist and `fbValtype`'s
// bounds guard rejected one stage earlier), and the floor was added because exactly one
// census cell of 250,238 went `loud emit reject` -> `check-clean invalid wasm` without it.
//
// WHY IT LIFTS (silent-class-inventory D244). The producer no longer reps as the box:
// `globalKind`'s `ObjLit` arm grew the rung `collectLocals` has carried since D51 — where
// the struct table has NO row for the shape (`collectS` keeps a union member out of it) the
// arm is the only nominal claimant, so the cell is the kind-8 variant. The value-call did
// not learn to build the arm; it is now handed one. The `@run` directive still catches a
// regression in either direction — a producer that reps as the box again fails this file
// whether the call site rejects it loudly or emits an invalid module.
//
// THE FLOOR'S OTHER TWO SHAPES ARE UNCHANGED AND STILL PINNED, each with its own file: a
// bare object LITERAL argument (`arm-param-value-call-objlit-arg-floor.vl`) and an
// `is Circle`-NARROWED union binding passed straight in
// (`arm-param-value-call-narrowed-arg-floor.vl`, added when this one graduated so the
// floor's coverage could not shrink silently). Both are `emitProgram: value-call union-ARM
// parameter given a value that is not that arm` before and after.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
const c = { r: 7 }
const lamc = (x: Circle) => x
const dd = lamc(c)
if (dd).r == 7 { print(7) } else { print(0) }
